  "quotes": [
    {
      "text": "Managed periods ==without any pain/cramps medication== for the ==first time in years==!",
      "who": "Travels a lot, trains around it",
      "month": "2026-02"
    },
    {
      "text": "Another cycle ==without painkillers==!!! Really grateful to you!",
      "who": "Travels a lot, trains around it",
      "month": "2026-03"
    },
    {
      "text": "Got some really nice photos in the beach vacation! ==Finally happy with how my body looks== and strength in general",
      "who": "Travels a lot, trains around it",
      "month": "2026-06"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yessssss. ==Hitting PRs== almost in every sesh.",
      "who": "Travels a lot, trains around it",
      "month": "2026-07"
    },
    {
      "text": "Managed to do a very random, ==unassisted pull up== with the worst form :D",
      "who": "Travels a lot, trains around it",
      "month": "2026-03"
    },
    {
      "text": "My daughter is almost 4 years old. I remember previously I used to have a back ache when carrying her. ==I don't anymore== and it feels great.",
      "who": "Dad of a four-year-old",
      "month": "2026-02"
    },
    {
      "text": "We did a long hike for mother's day and my daughter was tired. I was able to ==carry her on the way back== and did not feel strained.",
      "who": "Dad of a four-year-old",
      "month": "2026-05"
    },
    {
      "text": "My brother needed help moving a heavy piece of furniture up to the first floor and I helped him. He told me I ==wouldn't have been able to do this a few months ago==.",
      "who": "Dad of a four-year-old",
      "month": "2026-05"
    },
    {
      "text": "Today I ==lifted my wife in my arms==. I've never been able to do that. She mentioned I haven't ever had this much strength.",
      "who": "Dad of a four-year-old",
      "month": "2026-05"
    },
    {
      "text": "A lot of my clothes fit me really well and I ==feel confident== in front of other people.",
      "who": "Dad of a four-year-old",
      "month": "2026-02"
    },
    {
      "text": "==Six body weight pull ups== is a big milestone. I couldn't believe how much strength I have gained.",
      "who": "Dad of a four-year-old",
      "month": "2026-05"
    },
    {
      "text": "My wife mentioned that she could feel ==muscles on my side and back== which weren't there before.",
      "who": "Dad of a four-year-old",
      "month": "2026-06"
    },
    {
      "text": "Starting to ==enjoy going to the gym== because I never liked it.",
      "who": "Never liked the gym, until now",
      "month": "2026-01"
    },
    {
      "text": "I've started understanding how the weights at the gym work so I'm ==really enjoying it== compared to how I felt about weight lifting before.",
      "who": "Never liked the gym, until now",
      "month": "2026-02"
    },
    {
      "text": "All my health trends are ==moving in the positive direction== including heart rate, respiratory rate, active energy etc. so I'm happy and motivated.",
      "who": "Never liked the gym, until now",
      "month": "2026-03"
    },
    {
      "text": "I feel that I can break into a sprint immediately with Gabru and I would always hate running before, but ==now I often run with him== in the park",
      "who": "Runs in the park with her puppy",
      "month": "2026-01"
    },
    {
      "text": "Periods are ==back to regular==, hormone tests have come back fine",
      "who": "Runs in the park with her puppy",
      "month": "2025-12"
    },
    {
      "text": "Last week hit ==new PRs== - unlocked 22kg snatch, 35kg front squat",
      "who": "Runs in the park with her puppy",
      "month": "2026-01"
    },
    {
      "text": "This is the ==lowest weight in Decade==… achieving 84.8 makes me feel confident… 83 is just mid goal for me. I don't want to stop at that.",
      "who": "Lightest he's been in a decade",
      "month": "2026-05"
    },
    {
      "text": "Weight staying same but ==felt leaner==. Family and friends did confirm this.",
      "who": "Lightest he's been in a decade",
      "month": "2026-04"
    },
    {
      "text": "==First time== I was able to complete all 3 sets of hanging leg raises with 10 reps each",
      "who": "Full-time job plus weekend classes",
      "month": "2026-03"
    },
    {
      "text": "I followed your advice from last time about starting with higher weights, and it helped me ==hit PRs in multiple exercises==. Overall, lifting heavier also felt really good and gave me a nice boost.",
      "who": "Full-time job plus weekend classes",
      "month": "2026-06"
    },
    {
      "text": "==Much better knee pain== (and feeling of strength around it)",
      "who": "Cyclist in his thirties",
      "month": "2026-03"
    },
    {
      "text": "Back to gym sessions and can lift even higher weights. Could do ==2 pull ups and 3 chin ups== (bodyweight)",
      "who": "Racquet sports plus three gym days",
      "month": "2026-03"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lifting same weight but I don't feel muscle soreness as much and have the ==energy for the rest of the day==",
      "who": "Has energy left for the rest of the day",
      "month": "2026-04"
    },
    {
      "text": "I ==almost did 1 pull up== yesterday",
      "who": "Wants to build, not shrink",
      "month": "2026-08"
    },
    {
      "text": "Went to park and able to ==jog around 2km non stop==.",
      "who": "Forty-one and jogging again",
      "month": "2026-08"
    }
  ],
